      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "Position in labour depends mostly on women's preferences, and is chosen instinctively in order to reduce labour pain. Between two different positions: vertical and horizontal, the first of them seems to guarantee more convenient gas exchange in maternal lungs."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "To prove that the vertical position in labour increase spirometry parameters in comparison with horizontal one."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Women were divided into two groups according to position in labour and spirometry examination were performed in second period of labour. Group I were composed of 17 women in vertical position whereas group II--19 women in horizontal one."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Whole of analysed spirometral parameters had higher values in group I (8.2%-17.1%), but the increase wasn't statistically significant (p < 0.05)."
        }
      ]},
